    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script uses Schnakenberg's kinetics, the steady state, the Jacobian, and sigma(k) as the larger eigenvalue of J - k^2 D. k_c = (det/(Du Dv))^1/4 is the band-center formula; the measured argmax of sigma sits at 0.485 against k_c = 0.473, and that shift is reported. Parameters are a calibration to 0.0002006 m, not numbers from a Schnakenberg table for Aurelia. Five Lean theorems check the scaled discriminant, the equal-diffusion failure, and the 201 µm label identity, with no sorry." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion fit: Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 0.017, KS = 0.167 against a zero-discrepancy reference. Patch FFT wavelength 0.0002027 m versus assigned 0.0002006 m. Specimen foreground fraction 0.437, coherency 0.345 versus 0.849 on the spot field, bell circularity 0.328 versus a circle at 1. Those specimen numbers are measured, and the bell mask is a poor description of the round oral view (circularity 0.33). The lobe counter returned 5. Its reference was set to 8 rather than to the four gonads, which avoids a self-comparison but compares the wrong integer." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dv-sweep-wavelength-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-control-final-std>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-most-unstable-wavenumber-from-the-pde>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ocellus-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-contour-gonad-lobes>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-bell-circularity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-structure-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-spot-diameter-cv>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — MorphoEval overall 82.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements the Schnakenberg system at the Holocene 201 µm node (chronoseries 1/1, age 0 Ma). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 0.017, KS = 0.167. FFT wavelength on the patch is 202.7 µm against the assigned 200.6 µm. Equal diffusion gives sigma_max = -0.102 and final std = 3e-5, but the comparison panel autoscales that residual into a visible gradient. The upper-right bell mask has circularity 0.33, which does not describe the round medusa in the photograph. Gonad-lobe counter returned 5. Overall 82.2. Overall 82.2/100 (faithfulness 80.3, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 70, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 386216 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 4dfffe223a1b5f24a86aa2eb7bb7a2d3be3e5bcb5d0c43d979eba8266dcf20bc (sha256 4dfffe223a1b5f24a86aa2eb7bb7a2d3be3e5bcb5d0c43d979eba8266dcf20bc), spec_fingerprint 466a72b70c6deefab849cdaf54ef8ca2bbac24e0ab13e981975c600a6c11b298. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 466a72b70c6deefab849cdaf54ef8ca2bbac24e0ab13e981975c600a6c11b298; artifact_sha256: 4dfffe223a1b5f24a86aa2eb7bb7a2d3be3e5bcb5d0c43d979eba8266dcf20bc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/aurelia_aurita_specimen.jpg=f4f54dc98dc4d9b3..., datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=dad34a0a6b9d9a54..., datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=82e768a4e917def7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system can select a finite wavelength. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics implemented here. | Nakanishi, Hartenstein & Jacobs 2009: Aurelia rhopalia develop a pigment-cup ocellus. | Helm 2018: a scyphozoan medusa has eight rhopalia. | Thoma 2015 CC0 photograph of living Aurelia aurita.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=1, Dv=20, gamma=1, chosen so lambda_c equals 0.0002006 m. | Spectral integration, dispersion fit, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation.; transfer_boundary: 201 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a length measured on the photograph or in the cited papers.; does_not_claim: That eight rhopalia equal the bell circumference divided by 201 µm. | That the Karlsruhe photograph resolves the ocellus wavelength.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Draw the equal-diffusion field on the same color scale as the patterned activator so a std of 3e-5 cannot look like a stripe.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Replace the ragged upper-right mask (circularity 0.33) with a segmentation that follows the round oral bell.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Compare the lobe count to four gonads, not to eight rhopalia.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Second assessor from another provider has not scored this pass.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': '201 µm remains an assigned scale. No histological measurement was found; do not invent one.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.22e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dv from 12 to 48 moves predicted wavelength from 177 µm to 250 µm and the FFT peak follows it (sweep Pearson r = 0.9978). Spot count rises from 9 to 14 as the field saturates. Du = Dv = 1 kills the mode (sigma_max = -0.102, std = 3e-5). gamma and a, b are not swept. The control is numerically real and visually misleading." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — Reproducibility package: 86/100" ;
