<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — Morphological realism / specimen match: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Karlsruhe photograph is a real Aurelia (four-gonad oral bells, marginal tentacles). The activator panel is a spot field on a 602 µm patch, which is the right motif for an ocellus pigment pattern and the wrong magnification for the photograph. The equal-diffusion panel looks patterned because imshow autoscales a field whose standard deviation is 3e-5. The GIF's last frame is 90 percent the photograph, so computer-vision similarity is high for a reason that is not a pixel fit of the PDE to the bell." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/pass1_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): control panel shows a gradient; std in the title is 0.0000 — datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/pass1_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 386216 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 4dfffe223a1b5f24a86aa2eb7bb7a2d3be3e5bcb5d0c43d979eba8266dcf20bc (sha256 4dfffe223a1b5f24a86aa2eb7bb7a2d3be3e5bcb5d0c43d979eba8266dcf20bc), spec_fingerprint 466a72b70c6deefab849cdaf54ef8ca2bbac24e0ab13e981975c600a6c11b298",
        "models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py L449–L455: control imshow has no vmin/vmax shared with the patterned field <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L449-L455>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale (Aurelia aurita (moon jellyfish), Holocene, 0 Ma)",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale faithfully reproduces Aurelia aurita (moon jellyfish), Holocene, 0 Ma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Aurelia aurita (moon jellyfish), Holocene, 0 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Aurelia aurita (moon jellyfish), Holocene, 0 Ma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That eight rhopalia equal the bell circumference divided by 201 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Karlsruhe photograph resolves the ocellus wavelength.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral integration, dispersion fit, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=1, Dv=20, gamma=1, chosen so lambda_c equals 0.0002006 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Helm 2018: a scyphozoan medusa has eight rhopalia.",
        "reported_in_source: Nakanishi, Hartenstein & Jacobs 2009: Aurelia rhopalia develop a pigment-cup ocellus.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics implemented here.",
        "reported_in_source: Thoma 2015 CC0 photograph of living Aurelia aurita.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system can select a finite wavelength.",
        "transfer_boundary: 201 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a length measured on the photograph or in the cited papers." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Aurelia aurita" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Aurelia" ;
